  "rules": [
    "When sentiment is near zero (0.00-0.25) but recent history shows a sharp upward spike followed by volatility, the model systematically underestimates the immediate post-spike overshoot and fails to capture the subsequent mean-reversion phase.",
    "The model exhibits a strong lag in reacting to sudden price spikes; it assumes a smooth continuation rather than the volatile 'spike-and-mean-revert' pattern typical of EU ETS during high uncertainty periods.",
    "In low-sentiment environments, the model's 30-day forecast is biased toward a linear upward trend, ignoring the high probability of significant downside correction after initial rallies.",
    "The model consistently underestimates the amplitude of volatility when sentiment history contains isolated positive spikes (e.g., 0.25 or 0.50) amidst otherwise neutral data.",
    "Apply a downward correction to the forecasted trajectory if the true outcome shows a spike followed by a drop below the initial peak, indicating the model's linear projection is too optimistic."
  ]
}
